.TH PTY_ROW_TEXT 3 2026-10-03 "libptytest 0.1" "libptytest Manual"
.SH NAME
pty_row_text, pty_row_contains, pty_screen_contains, pty_screen_text,
pty_screen_is_blank \- read the screen as text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <ptytest.h>
.PP
.BI "char *pty_row_text(PtySession *" s ", int " row ", char *" buf ", size_t " size );
.BI "int pty_row_contains(PtySession *" s ", int " row ", const char *" text );
.BI "int pty_screen_contains(PtySession *" s ", const char *" text );
.BI "char *pty_screen_text(PtySession *" s ", char *" buf ", size_t " size );
.BI "int pty_screen_is_blank(PtySession *" s );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR pty_row_text ()
copies the text of
.I row
into
.IR buf :
every cell's character in column order (the second column of a wide
character contributes nothing), with trailing blanks removed and leading
blanks kept.
The result is always NUL-terminated and is truncated at a character
boundary if
.I size
is too small.
.PP
.BR pty_row_contains ()
and
.BR pty_screen_contains ()
search one row, or each row in turn, for
.I text
as a substring.
A match never spans two rows.
.PP
.BR pty_screen_text ()
copies the whole screen: one line per row as
.BR pty_row_text ()
gives it, separated by newlines, with no newline after the last row.
.PP
.BR pty_screen_is_blank ()
tells whether every cell holds a blank.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR pty_row_text ()
and
.BR pty_screen_text ()
return
.IR buf ;
for a row out of range the string is empty.
.BR pty_row_contains (),
.BR pty_screen_contains ()
and
.BR pty_screen_is_blank ()
return 1 or 0; a NULL session counts as blank and contains nothing.
.SH NOTES
"The text appears somewhere" tests content, not layout.
Use
.BR pty_screen_compare (3)
for every view at least once.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pty_screen_compare (3),
.BR pty_cell_text (3),
.BR pty_assert (3)
